  "slug": "mitochondrial-resource-16ed",
  "summary": "New atlases in mouse, sheep, pig and long-read databases extend regulatory maps below the gene level and across tissues and species.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is building tissue- and species-spanning regulatory resources with finer-than-gene resolution. The mouse atlas maps age-associated differential transcript usage across brain, liver, and adipose, finding predominantly regulatory isoform switching, with BioEMU modeling used to test structural consequences. IsoAPA catalogs 2.3M transcript-resolved polyadenylation sites from PacBio and Nanopore data across 816 sample groups. SheepGTEx links regulatory variants from 6,761 RNA-seq samples across 51 tissues to 34 complex traits, and the pig pan-genome adds T2T assemblies, structural variation and a pan-transcriptome for genotype-phenotype mapping. A commentary on conserved cell-type signatures is related to cross-species identity rather than isoforms. What is new is the extension of regulatory annotation to isoform and polyadenylation units and to livestock genomes.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
